    "detailed_description": "<i>Someone knocks on your door in the middle of the night. You go and check it out but no one is outside your apartment. You know something is wrong.</i><br><br><strong>Features</strong><br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>A Linear Story</strong> with a focus on exploration and taking around or within an hour to complete.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Atmospheric Environments</strong> crafted thoughtfully.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Free Roam Gamemode.</strong> Explore the entire game world at your own pace, without linear horror events impeding progress.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Minimal Gameplay Mechanics</strong> typical of 'walking simulator' genre.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Dynamic lighting.</strong> global illumination can be disabled in settings menu.</li></ul><br><i>Follows after the events of Where's Oswald.</i><br><br>There are no jump scares. Confront the past once more in One More Dream.<br><br><i>Note: The linear story is intended to be completed in one sitting and does not autosave.</i>",
